    "scientific_limitations": [
        "The target labels originate from the PB2002 boundary model rather than independent direct physical observations.",
        "Several predictive variables are PB2002-derived kinematic and geometric properties; the model therefore partly reconstructs the relationship between PB2002 metadata and PB2002 labels.",
        "Standard random stratified splitting allows earthquakes associated with the same continuous fault or trench to appear in both training and test partitions.",
        "Boundary-aware disjoint evaluation provides a more challenging out-of-boundary test, yielding a Macro F1 of 79.35% rather than 99.98%.",
        "TectonicSense is an environmental characterization and classification model; it is NOT an earthquake prediction or forecasting system.",
        "The results reflect empirical classification performance under the evaluated PB2002 feature configuration, not universal physical causality."
    ]
